{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"ff91daa7-3671-428b-aa4a-741e289da74b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to NCERT, what principle was intended to guide relations between the Centre and the States in India?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT के अनुसार भारत में केंद्र और राज्यों के संबंधों का मार्गदर्शन किस सिद्धांत से होना था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Permanent confrontation\",\"hi\":\"स्थायी टकराव\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Cooperation while recognising diversity and emphasising unity\",\"hi\":\"विविधता को मान्यता देते हुए और एकता पर बल देते हुए सहयोग\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Complete dependence of States on local bodies\",\"hi\":\"राज्यों की स्थानीय निकायों पर पूर्ण निर्भरता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Separate international sovereignty for every State\",\"hi\":\"हर राज्य की अलग अंतरराष्ट्रीय संप्रभुता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 156, 158, 164 and 172. Direct official document: NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ff33036c-979d-4033-b598-42e0370f5720\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"If difficulty arises in construing part of the Hindi translation under Article 394A, what does the Constitution require?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 394A के अधीन हिंदी अनुवाद के किसी भाग को समझने में कठिनाई उत्पन्न हो तो संविधान क्या अपेक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The translation automatically becomes void\",\"hi\":\"अनुवाद स्वतः शून्य हो जाता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The President must cause it to be suitably revised\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति उसका उपयुक्त पुनरीक्षण कराएँगे\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court must rewrite the entire Constitution\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय पूरे संविधान को पुनः लिखेगा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only Parliament may publish an unofficial summary\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद अनौपचारिक सार प्रकाशित कर सकती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 394A(2)-(3) (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ff03fac8-d64e-4c99-9dc0-73c97cb83088\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which list consists entirely of liberties expressly named in the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सी सूची पूरी तरह उन स्वतंत्रताओं से बनी है जिनका उद्देशिका में स्पष्ट उल्लेख है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Trade, movement, residence and profession\",\"hi\":\"व्यापार, संचरण, निवास और व्यवसाय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Property, contract, inheritance and taxation\",\"hi\":\"संपत्ति, संविदा, उत्तराधिकार और कराधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Press, association, assembly and petition\",\"hi\":\"प्रेस, संगठन, सभा और याचिका\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Thought, expression, belief, faith and worship\",\"hi\":\"विचार, अभिव्यक्ति, विश्वास, धर्म और उपासना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Preamble and Articles 19 and 25. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"febfe1c4-0b99-487a-bacb-0d0808a08473\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"The Union, State and Concurrent Lists are contained in which part of the constitutional scheme?\",\"hi\":\"संघ, राज्य और समवर्ती सूचियाँ संवैधानिक व्यवस्था के किस भाग में दी गई हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Fifth Schedule alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल पाँचवीं अनुसूची\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Seventh Schedule read with Article 246\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 246 के साथ पठित सातवीं अनुसूची\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Tenth Schedule read with Article 102\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 102 के साथ पठित दसवीं अनुसूची\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल प्रस्तावना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 246, PDF p. 175, and Seventh Schedule, Lists I-III, PDF pp. 340-353. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fe6278f4-0108-4978-97ab-e3a2037bc847\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to the verified NCERT source table, Law-making procedure is associated with which source?\",\"hi\":\"सत्यापित NCERT स्रोत-सारणी के अनुसार विधि-निर्माण प्रक्रिया किस स्रोत से संबंधित है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Irish Constitution\",\"hi\":\"आयरिश संविधान\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"British Constitution\",\"hi\":\"ब्रिटिश संविधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"French Constitution\",\"hi\":\"फ्रांसीसी संविधान\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Canadian Constitution\",\"hi\":\"कनाडाई संविधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class XI, source table, printed p. 22; Constitution of India, relevant provisions. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf ; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India, as on 1 May 2026 — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fd829549-ad85-46c2-8d26-02bc21786651\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court’s discretionary power to grant special leave to appeal is found in:\",\"hi\":\"अपील की विशेष अनुमति देने की सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की विवेकाधीन शक्ति किसमें है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 136\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 136\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 129\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 129\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 143\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 143\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 214\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 214\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 136(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fb557157-579a-40c0-95e8-1c20331e66f0\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which preserved record explains the reasoning behind constitutional provisions and assists interpretation?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा संरक्षित अभिलेख संवैधानिक प्रावधानों के पीछे का तर्क बताता और व्याख्या में सहायता करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Supreme Court Reports\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय रिपोर्ट्स\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Cabinet Mission Statement\",\"hi\":\"कैबिनेट मिशन वक्तव्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Government of India Act, 1935 alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल भारत शासन अधिनियम, 1935\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Constituent Assembly Debates\",\"hi\":\"संविधान सभा वाद-विवाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class IX, printed p. 25. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2 “Constitutional Design”, Reprint 2025-26 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf ; NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fb2a8ec6-3a07-4be6-9aff-845850f00fbd\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 139A allows the Supreme Court, in specified circumstances, to:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 139A निर्दिष्ट परिस्थितियों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को क्या करने देता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Withdraw certain cases involving the same or substantially the same questions of law from High Courts and dispose of them itself, and transfer cases between High Courts\",\"hi\":\"समान या पर्याप्त रूप से समान विधि-प्रश्न वाले कुछ मामले उच्च न्यायालयों से वापस लेकर स्वयं निपटाना तथा उच्च न्यायालयों के बीच मामले स्थानांतरित करना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Appoint all district judges without consultation\",\"hi\":\"बिना परामर्श सभी जिला न्यायाधीश नियुक्त करना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Abolish the High Courts by judicial order\",\"hi\":\"न्यायिक आदेश से उच्च न्यायालय समाप्त करना\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Create separate State constitutions\",\"hi\":\"अलग राज्य संविधान बनाना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 139A(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"faf5f8dc-6130-4c95-ac31-952e49bd88c3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 7 generally addresses persons who migrated from India to Pakistan after which date?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 7 सामान्यतः उन व्यक्तियों से संबंधित है जो किस तारीख के बाद भारत से पाकिस्तान गए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"15 August 1947\",\"hi\":\"15 अगस्त 1947\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 March 1947\",\"hi\":\"1 मार्च 1947\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"19 July 1948\",\"hi\":\"19 जुलाई 1948\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"26 January 1950\",\"hi\":\"26 जनवरी 1950\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 7, opening words, PDF p. 35. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fa991b67-35e7-456d-be62-556b7f95ea74\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Assertion (A): A written Constitution can remain a “living document.”\\nReason (R): Its written text may be amended and interpreted while retaining an identifiable constitutional framework.\",\"hi\":\"अभिकथन (A): लिखित संविधान “जीवंत दस्तावेज” बना रह सकता है।\\nकारण (R): पहचान योग्य संवैधानिक ढाँचा बनाए रखते हुए उसके लिखित पाठ में संशोधन और उसकी व्याख्या की जा सकती है।\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A\",\"hi\":\"A और R दोनों सही हैं तथा R, A की सही व्याख्या है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A\",\"hi\":\"A और R दोनों सही हैं, किंतु R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A is true, but R is false\",\"hi\":\"A सही है, किंतु R गलत है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A is false, but R is true\",\"hi\":\"A गलत है, किंतु R सही है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 9, pp. 196-200 and 212-215 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps209.pdf); Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Contents and amendment footnotes (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f92dc187-0595-4f42-a0b3-3f2c0edc8d1a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Before Parliament can create a new All India Service under Article 312, Rajya Sabha must declare that it is necessary or expedient in the national interest by:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 312 के अधीन संसद नई अखिल भारतीय सेवा बनाए, उससे पहले राज्यसभा को राष्ट्रीय हित में इसकी आवश्यकता या समीचीनता किस बहुमत से घोषित करनी होती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Not less than two-thirds of members present and voting\",\"hi\":\"उपस्थित और मतदान करने वाले सदस्यों के कम-से-कम दो-तिहाई\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A simple majority of Lok Sabha alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल लोकसभा का साधारण बहुमत\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Unanimous consent of all State Legislatures\",\"hi\":\"सभी राज्य विधानमंडलों की सर्वसम्मति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A majority of the Supreme Court judges\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों का बहुमत\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 312(1)-(2), PDF p. 205. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f91a0fa7-9a27-48e4-826f-4cddfa689cd3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which description best captures the constitutional design of Indian federalism?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा वर्णन भारतीय संघवाद की संवैधानिक रचना को सबसे अच्छी तरह व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Independent sovereign States joined only by treaty\",\"hi\":\"केवल संधि से जुड़े स्वतंत्र संप्रभु राज्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A wholly unitary system with no constitutional State sphere\",\"hi\":\"राज्यों के संवैधानिक क्षेत्र के बिना पूर्ण एकात्मक व्यवस्था\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A confederation whose central authority depends on State permission\",\"hi\":\"ऐसा परिसंघ जिसकी केंद्रीय सत्ता राज्य अनुमति पर निर्भर है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A federal division of powers combined with significant Union-strengthening provisions\",\"hi\":\"शक्तियों का संघीय विभाजन तथा संघ को मजबूत करने वाले महत्त्वपूर्ण प्रावधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 158-163; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Articles 3, 246, 248 and 353, PDF pp. 32-33, 175-176 and 240-241. Direct official documents: NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf); Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8ffc9ad-b9c5-45f3-a05c-84e677095497\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"If the President asks the Council of Ministers to reconsider its advice under Article 74, what follows after reconsideration?\",\"hi\":\"यदि राष्ट्रपति अनुच्छेद 74 के अधीन मंत्रिपरिषद को अपनी सलाह पर पुनर्विचार करने को कहें, तो पुनर्विचार के बाद क्या होता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The President may reject the advice permanently\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति सलाह को स्थायी रूप से अस्वीकार कर सकते हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court chooses the final policy\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय अंतिम नीति चुनता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A referendum becomes compulsory\",\"hi\":\"जनमत-संग्रह अनिवार्य हो जाता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The President must act according to the advice tendered after reconsideration\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति को पुनर्विचार के बाद दी गई सलाह के अनुसार कार्य करना होता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), proviso to Article 74(1), PDF p. 64. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 4, Executive, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 88-89. Direct official documents: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Class 11, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 4 Executive (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps204.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8c60dfb-f70b-4250-becb-1c3557200ef1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which body was the formal maker of the Constitution of India?\",\"hi\":\"भारत के संविधान का औपचारिक निर्माता कौन-सा निकाय था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Drafting Committee acting alone\",\"hi\":\"अकेले कार्यरत प्रारूप समिति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"British Parliament\",\"hi\":\"ब्रिटिश संसद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Constituent Assembly\",\"hi\":\"संविधान सभा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Federal Court of India\",\"hi\":\"भारत का संघीय न्यायालय\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class IX, printed p. 24; Constitution, commencement note. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2 “Constitutional Design”, Reprint 2025-26 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf ; NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf ; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India, as on 1 May 2026 — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f53720e0-fe64-4294-a23a-3df2d00636d4\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 326 bases elections to the House of the People and State Legislative Assemblies on:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 326 लोक सभा और राज्य विधान सभाओं के चुनाव किस आधार पर रखता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary nomination\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत नामांकन\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Property ownership\",\"hi\":\"संपत्ति स्वामित्व\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Educational qualification alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल शैक्षिक योग्यता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Adult suffrage\",\"hi\":\"वयस्क मताधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 326. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 3, Election and Representation, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 67-68. Direct official documents: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Chapter 3, Election and Representation (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps203.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f4cb5a7b-a523-4f1e-860e-8b13dcae1d46\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly describes the legal status of the Hindi text published under Article 394A?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 394A के अधीन प्रकाशित हिंदी पाठ की कानूनी स्थिति का सही वर्णन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It is merely a private study aid\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल निजी अध्ययन-सहायिका है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It is advisory only for State Governments\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल राज्य सरकारों के लिए परामर्शात्मक है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It is deemed the authoritative Hindi text for all purposes\",\"hi\":\"इसे सभी प्रयोजनों के लिए प्राधिकृत हिंदी पाठ माना जाता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It applies only to the Preamble\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल प्रस्तावना पर लागू होता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 394A(1)-(3) (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f383f3a0-267c-4135-ae55-b141a7187ecc\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Schedule demonstrates that the written Constitution contains three legislative lists?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सी अनुसूची दर्शाती है कि लिखित संविधान में तीन विधायी सूचियाँ हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Third Schedule\",\"hi\":\"तीसरी अनुसूची\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Seventh Schedule\",\"hi\":\"सातवीं अनुसूची\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Eighth Schedule\",\"hi\":\"आठवीं अनुसूची\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Tenth Schedule\",\"hi\":\"दसवीं अनुसूची\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 246 and Seventh Schedule—Union, State and Concurrent Lists (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f30a8b7d-12e4-43ea-bd74-ed65a3c1b76f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Article guarantees the right to move the Supreme Court for enforcement of Fundamental Rights?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा अनुच्छेद मौलिक अधिकारों के प्रवर्तन के लिए सर्वोच्च न्यायालय जाने के अधिकार की गारंटी देता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 21\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 21\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 32\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 32\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 136\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 136\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 226\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 226\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 32(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f2c615c7-7ce9-4841-8ff9-3a80d556d385\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly describes the role of an affected State Legislature under the proviso to Article 3?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 3 के परंतुक के अधीन प्रभावित राज्य विधानमंडल की भूमिका का सही वर्णन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Its unanimous consent is constitutionally mandatory\",\"hi\":\"उसकी सर्वसम्मत सहमति संवैधानिक रूप से अनिवार्य है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The President refers the Bill for its views within a specified period; its consent is not made binding\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति विधेयक को निर्धारित अवधि में उसके विचारों के लिए भेजते हैं; उसकी सहमति को बाध्यकारी नहीं बनाया गया है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It may itself amend the First Schedule\",\"hi\":\"वह स्वयं पहली अनुसूची में संशोधन कर सकता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It decides the Bill by referendum\",\"hi\":\"वह जनमत-संग्रह से विधेयक तय करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), proviso to Article 3, PDF p. 33; Supreme Court of India, In Re: Article 370 of the Constitution, judgment dated 11 December 2023, paragraphs 510-511, PDF pp. 344-346. Direct official documents: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); Supreme Court of India, In Re: Article 370, judgment dated 11 December 2023 (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/29796/29796_2019_1_1501_49019_Judgement_11-Dec-2023.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f234adbb-bebb-48f2-95a3-330a2efc5e2a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 75(1B) bars which person from being appointed a Union Minister for the constitutionally specified period?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 75(1B) संवैधानिक रूप से निर्दिष्ट अवधि तक किस व्यक्ति को संघीय मंत्री नियुक्त होने से रोकता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every defeated election candidate\",\"hi\":\"हर पराजित चुनाव प्रत्याशी\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every former civil servant\",\"hi\":\"हर पूर्व लोक सेवक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A member disqualified under paragraph 2 of the Tenth Schedule\",\"hi\":\"दसवीं अनुसूची के पैरा 2 के अधीन अयोग्य घोषित सदस्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Every member of Rajya Sabha\",\"hi\":\"राज्यसभा का हर सदस्य\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 75(1B) and Tenth Schedule, paragraph 2, PDF pp. 65 and 375-376. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f1152a60-eeab-4827-9525-ac625c88d7f9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 88, a Minister who is not a member of a particular House may:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 88 के अधीन किसी विशेष सदन का सदस्य न होने वाला मंत्री क्या कर सकता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Vote there solely because of ministerial office\",\"hi\":\"केवल मंत्री-पद के कारण वहाँ मतदान कर सकता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Preside permanently over that House\",\"hi\":\"उस सदन की स्थायी अध्यक्षता कर सकता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Dissolve that House personally\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्तिगत रूप से उस सदन को भंग कर सकता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Speak and take part in its proceedings but not vote there merely by virtue of Article 88\",\"hi\":\"उसकी कार्यवाही में बोल और भाग ले सकता है, पर केवल अनुच्छेद 88 के आधार पर वहाँ मतदान नहीं कर सकता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 88, PDF p. 71. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f057a9cf-1112-4f1e-9e7f-a46f32edad94\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How does an integrated judiciary differ from a dual judicial system?\",\"hi\":\"एकीकृत न्यायपालिका दोहरी न्यायिक व्यवस्था से कैसे भिन्न होती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It abolishes all State-level courts\",\"hi\":\"यह राज्य स्तर के सभी न्यायालय समाप्त कर देती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It links Union and State-level courts in one hierarchy instead of maintaining wholly separate federal and State court systems\",\"hi\":\"यह पूर्णतः अलग संघीय और राज्य न्यायालय प्रणालियों के बजाय संघ और राज्य स्तर के न्यायालयों को एक पदानुक्रम में जोड़ती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It prevents every court from applying Central laws\",\"hi\":\"यह प्रत्येक न्यायालय को केंद्रीय कानून लागू करने से रोकती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It removes appellate review from the judiciary\",\"hi\":\"यह न्यायपालिका से अपीलीय समीक्षा हटा देती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Articles 132-136 and 141. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 6, Judiciary, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 131-134, integrated hierarchy and appellate jurisdiction. Direct official documents: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Class 11, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 6 Judiciary (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps206.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ee87f1a0-8d12-4fd6-8913-9f2978244d13\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"At the State level, the Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the:\",\"hi\":\"राज्य स्तर पर मंत्रिपरिषद सामूहिक रूप से किसके प्रति उत्तरदायी है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Legislative Council alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल विधान परिषद\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Legislative Assembly of the State\",\"hi\":\"राज्य की विधान सभा\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Governor personally\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्तिगत रूप से राज्यपाल\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"High Court\",\"hi\":\"उच्च न्यायालय\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 164(2), PDF p. 103. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ee533992-2187-4401-9f41-39de20192911\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"At the Union level, collective responsibility of the Council of Ministers is constitutionally owed to:\",\"hi\":\"संघ स्तर पर मंत्रिपरिषद की सामूहिक उत्तरदायित्व संवैधानिक रूप से किसके प्रति है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Council of States alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल राज्यों की परिषद्\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Election Commission\",\"hi\":\"निर्वाचन आयोग\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The House of the People\",\"hi\":\"लोक सभा\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 75(3). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ec48a0c0-4b62-4446-84fe-8b17aef4b855\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How many Schedules are listed in the official Constitution edition updated through the 106th Amendment?\",\"hi\":\"106वें संशोधन तक अद्यतन आधिकारिक संविधान संस्करण में कितनी अनुसूचियाँ सूचीबद्ध हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Twelve\",\"hi\":\"बारह\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Eight\",\"hi\":\"आठ\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Ten\",\"hi\":\"दस\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Twenty-two\",\"hi\":\"बाईस\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Preface and Contents—First through Twelfth Schedules (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e7d82267-dc01-42db-a799-711cd4110765\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Article authorises a Proclamation when the financial stability or credit of India or any part of its territory is threatened?\",\"hi\":\"भारत या उसके राज्यक्षेत्र के किसी भाग की वित्तीय स्थायित्व या साख को खतरा होने पर कौन-सा अनुच्छेद उद्घोषणा अधिकृत करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 360\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 360\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 324\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 324\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 263\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 263\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 123\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 123\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 360(1). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e7cba97f-cbcc-45f9-9128-ad3e86600b61\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Equality in the Preamble is expressed as equality of:\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका में समानता को किसकी समानता के रूप में व्यक्त किया गया है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Status and opportunity\",\"hi\":\"प्रतिष्ठा और अवसर\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Income and property in every case\",\"hi\":\"हर मामले में आय और संपत्ति\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Office and seniority only\",\"hi\":\"केवल पद और वरिष्ठता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Language and territory only\",\"hi\":\"केवल भाषा और राज्यक्षेत्र\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Preamble. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e386f35a-2ad2-4c24-bcc6-7518ea222c49\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which source-pair correctly distinguishes justiciable rights from non-justiciable directives?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा स्रोत-युग्म न्यायालय द्वारा प्रवर्तनीय अधिकारों और अप्रवर्तनीय निर्देशों का सही अंतर करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Ireland — Fundamental Rights; Britain — Directive Principles\",\"hi\":\"आयरलैंड — मौलिक अधिकार; ब्रिटेन — नीति-निदेशक तत्व\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Canada — Fundamental Rights; France — Directive Principles\",\"hi\":\"कनाडा — मौलिक अधिकार; फ्रांस — नीति-निदेशक तत्व\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"France — Fundamental Rights; United States — Directive Principles\",\"hi\":\"फ्रांस — मौलिक अधिकार; संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका — नीति-निदेशक तत्व\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"United States — Fundamental Rights; Ireland — Directive Principles\",\"hi\":\"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका — मौलिक अधिकार; आयरलैंड — नीति-निदेशक तत्व\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class XI, source table, printed p. 22; Constitution, Articles 32 and 37. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf ; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India, as on 1 May 2026 — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e3680651-cf55-42d6-944b-b72995f27636\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does single citizenship mean in the Indian constitutional system?\",\"hi\":\"भारतीय संवैधानिक व्यवस्था में एकल नागरिकता का क्या अर्थ है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A person holds Indian citizenship, not a separate constitutional citizenship of an individual State\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्ति भारतीय नागरिकता रखता है, किसी अलग राज्य की पृथक संवैधानिक नागरिकता नहीं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only one person in a family may be a citizen\",\"hi\":\"एक परिवार में केवल एक व्यक्ति नागरिक हो सकता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A citizen may live in only one State throughout life\",\"hi\":\"नागरिक जीवनभर केवल एक राज्य में रह सकता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"State Governments independently grant national citizenship\",\"hi\":\"राज्य सरकारें स्वतंत्र रूप से राष्ट्रीय नागरिकता देती हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Part II, Articles 5-11, PDF pp. 34-36. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 154-155. Direct official documents: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Chapter 7 Federalism (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e1f7d37a-394b-4c96-9f1c-c965e349a815\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which arrangement is a basic feature of a federal system?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सी व्यवस्था संघीय प्रणाली की मूल विशेषता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"All governmental power belongs to local bodies\",\"hi\":\"सारी सरकारी शक्ति स्थानीय निकायों में होती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Regional governments exist only by executive permission\",\"hi\":\"क्षेत्रीय सरकारें केवल कार्यपालिका की अनुमति से रहती हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"National and regional governments have constitutionally assigned spheres\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रीय और क्षेत्रीय सरकारों के संवैधानिक रूप से निर्धारित क्षेत्र होते हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only one level of government has constitutional status\",\"hi\":\"केवल एक स्तर की सरकार को संवैधानिक दर्जा होता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 155-156. Direct official document: NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e13155e0-ced6-4681-b3f0-06577c913390\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which structural unit of the Constitution is explicitly divided into Chapters in several Parts?\",\"hi\":\"संविधान की कौन-सी संरचनात्मक इकाई कई भागों में स्पष्ट रूप से अध्यायों में विभाजित है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the Preamble\",\"hi\":\"केवल प्रस्तावना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Parts such as Part V and Part VI\",\"hi\":\"भाग V और भाग VI जैसे भाग\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Every Schedule without exception\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक अनुसूची बिना अपवाद\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only the list of abbreviations\",\"hi\":\"केवल संक्षेपों की सूची\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Contents—Part V and Part VI chapter structure (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"de712c27-72db-4a92-bffe-ad952d9f9fe8\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What limit does Article 164(1A) place on the size of a State Council of Ministers?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 164(1A) राज्य मंत्रिपरिषद के आकार पर कौन-सी सीमा लगाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Not more than fifteen per cent of Assembly membership, with a minimum of twelve Ministers\",\"hi\":\"विधानसभा सदस्यता के पंद्रह प्रतिशत से अधिक नहीं, पर न्यूनतम बारह मंत्री\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Exactly ten Ministers in every State\",\"hi\":\"हर राज्य में ठीक दस मंत्री\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"One-half of the Legislative Council\",\"hi\":\"विधान परिषद का आधा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"No constitutional maximum or minimum\",\"hi\":\"कोई संवैधानिक अधिकतम या न्यूनतम सीमा नहीं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 164(1A), PDF p. 103. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"dca73e00-9260-41a5-9c2a-81a739cd2667\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 77(1), executive action of the Government of India is expressed to be taken in the name of the:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 77(1) के अधीन भारत सरकार की कार्यपालिका कार्रवाई किसके नाम से की गई व्यक्त होती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Prime Minister personally\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्तिगत रूप से प्रधानमंत्री\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Parliament\",\"hi\":\"संसद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"President\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Supreme Court\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 77(1), PDF p. 67. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"dc461fe8-acf4-489f-841d-45d1dffe9b28\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 30(1) gives which minorities the right to establish and administer educational institutions of their choice?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 30(1) किन अल्पसंख्यकों को अपनी पसंद की शैक्षणिक संस्थाएँ स्थापित और प्रशासित करने का अधिकार देता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Minorities based on religion or language\",\"hi\":\"धर्म या भाषा पर आधारित अल्पसंख्यक\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only occupational minorities\",\"hi\":\"केवल व्यावसायिक अल्पसंख्यक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only temporary political coalitions\",\"hi\":\"केवल अस्थायी राजनीतिक गठबंधन\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only residents of one municipality\",\"hi\":\"केवल एक नगरपालिका के निवासी\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 30(1). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d86ad37f-a0d3-4b50-9382-3ea079af4e55\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A person claims an unrestricted constitutional right to practise religion even when public health is endangered. Which statement is correct under Article 25(1)?\",\"hi\":\"कोई व्यक्ति जन-स्वास्थ्य को खतरा होने पर भी धर्म के आचरण के असीमित संवैधानिक अधिकार का दावा करता है। अनुच्छेद 25(1) के अधीन सही कथन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The right is absolute against every constitutional limitation\",\"hi\":\"अधिकार प्रत्येक संवैधानिक सीमा के विरुद्ध निरपेक्ष है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Freedom of conscience and religious profession, practice and propagation is subject to public order, morality, health and the other provisions of Part III\",\"hi\":\"अंतःकरण तथा धर्म को मानने, आचरण और प्रचार की स्वतंत्रता लोक व्यवस्था, सदाचार, स्वास्थ्य और भाग III के अन्य प्रावधानों के अधीन है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 25 protects only government departments\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 25 केवल सरकारी विभागों की रक्षा करता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Constitution recognises no freedom of conscience\",\"hi\":\"संविधान अंतःकरण की स्वतंत्रता नहीं मानता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 25(1). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d7f562b4-eff0-47e7-9476-ae3b08b0b83b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Every High Court is a court of record under:\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक उच्च न्यायालय किसके अधीन अभिलेख न्यायालय है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 214\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 214\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 226\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 226\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 215\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 215\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 235\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 235\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 215. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d7e1f6e5-526e-4861-83ca-63d3b0baa378\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which proposition is consistent with NCERT’s discussion of how constitutional rules may be organised?\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक नियमों की व्यवस्था के बारे में NCERT की चर्चा से कौन-सा निष्कर्ष संगत है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every country must have one single document called the Constitution\",\"hi\":\"हर देश में संविधान नाम का एक ही दस्तावेज होना आवश्यक है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Constitutional rules may be consolidated in one instrument or distributed across several sources that together perform the constitutional role\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक नियम एक दस्तावेज में समेकित हो सकते हैं या कई स्रोतों में वितरित हो सकते हैं जो मिलकर संवैधानिक भूमिका निभाते हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only democratic countries can have constitutions\",\"hi\":\"केवल लोकतांत्रिक देशों में संविधान हो सकता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A constitution contains procedures but never values\",\"hi\":\"संविधान में प्रक्रियाएँ होती हैं, किंतु मूल्य कभी नहीं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 1, pp. 3, 8, 10 and 22-23 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d7c6f592-bf6d-4521-984b-9d35d6b3b254\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following enactments:\\n1. Indian Independence Act, 1947\\n2. Government of India Act, 1935\\nWhich were expressly repealed by Article 395?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित अधिनियमों पर विचार कीजिए:\\n1. भारतीय स्वतंत्रता अधिनियम, 1947\\n2. भारत शासन अधिनियम, 1935\\nअनुच्छेद 395 ने किन्हें स्पष्ट रूप से निरस्त किया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"2 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Neither 1 nor 2\",\"hi\":\"न तो 1, न ही 2\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Both 1 and 2\",\"hi\":\"1 और 2 दोनों\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 395—repeal of the Indian Independence Act, 1947 and Government of India Act, 1935 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d71b727a-9b5c-4aa9-8d0a-729e211cdae3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Who appoints the Prime Minister under Article 75(1)?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 75(1) के अधीन प्रधानमंत्री की नियुक्ति कौन करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"President\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Chief Justice of India\",\"hi\":\"भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Election Commission\",\"hi\":\"निर्वाचन आयोग\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Rajya Sabha Chairman\",\"hi\":\"राज्यसभा सभापति\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 75(1), PDF p. 65. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 4, Executive, 2026-27 reprint, printed p. 90. Direct official documents: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Class 11, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 4 Executive (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps204.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d6aa83f8-c381-4b89-932d-49c454261e25\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which commitment was common to both the 1928 draft and the 1931 Karachi Resolution?\",\"hi\":\"1928 के प्रारूप और 1931 के कराची प्रस्ताव—दोनों में कौन-सी प्रतिबद्धता समान थी?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A permanently restricted franchise\",\"hi\":\"स्थायी रूप से सीमित मताधिकार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Universal adult franchise\",\"hi\":\"सार्वभौमिक वयस्क मताधिकार\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A hereditary head as the source of authority\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत प्रमुख को अधिकार का स्रोत बनाना\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Exclusion of minority-rights safeguards\",\"hi\":\"अल्पसंख्यक-अधिकार सुरक्षा को बाहर रखना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class IX, printed p. 23. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2 “Constitutional Design”, Reprint 2025-26 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf ; NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d5303a39-ead1-46e0-90d3-9d55aa880749\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 356 concerns a situation in which the President is satisfied that:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 356 उस स्थिति से संबंधित है जिसमें राष्ट्रपति का समाधान हो कि:\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every State budget must be written by Parliament\",\"hi\":\"हर राज्य बजट संसद लिखे\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"All High Courts should be temporarily abolished\",\"hi\":\"सभी उच्च न्यायालय अस्थायी रूप से समाप्त हों\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A State requests a separate citizenship\",\"hi\":\"कोई राज्य अलग नागरिकता माँगे\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The government of a State cannot be carried on in accordance with the Constitution\",\"hi\":\"किसी राज्य का शासन संविधान के उपबंधों के अनुसार नहीं चलाया जा सकता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 356(1). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d4d614c1-e416-4000-a3c6-79046bcec917\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly describes High Court writ jurisdiction under Article 226?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 226 के अधीन उच्च न्यायालय की रिट अधिकारिता का सही वर्णन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It is confined to disputes between States\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल राज्यों के बीच विवादों तक सीमित है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It applies only after Supreme Court permission\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की अनुमति के बाद लागू होती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It cannot enforce Fundamental Rights\",\"hi\":\"यह मौलिक अधिकार लागू नहीं कर सकती\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It extends to enforcement of Fundamental Rights and to any other purpose within its constitutional scope\",\"hi\":\"यह अपने संवैधानिक दायरे में मौलिक अधिकारों के प्रवर्तन और किसी अन्य प्रयोजन तक फैली है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 226(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d49770f9-149e-43ad-b9ef-1f8d63626842\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which of the following Articles was expressly brought into force “at once” by Article 394?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित में से किस अनुच्छेद को अनुच्छेद 394 द्वारा स्पष्ट रूप से “तत्काल” लागू किया गया था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 324\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 324\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 368\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 368\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 352\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 352\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 280\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 280\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 394—immediate-operation list including Article 324 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d32566b8-8ca0-4917-b5d7-422295809159\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to the verified NCERT source table, Firs